<html xmlns:o="urn:schemas-microsoft-com:office:office"
      xmlns:w="urn:schemas-microsoft-com:office:word"
      xmlns="http://www.w3.org/TR/REC-html40">
<head>
  <meta charset="UTF-8"/>
  <title>HUM.org SQL login system</title>
  <!--[if gte mso 9]><xml><w:WordDocument><w:View>Print</w:View></w:WordDocument></xml><![endif]-->
</head>
<body>
  <h1>HUM.org SQL login system</h1>
  <p>Open this file in Word or another word processor. It describes the lab login desk that lives under <code>site/login/</code>.</p>
  <h2>Advice</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Use SQLite here. The HUM repo already treats SQLite as the local database. You do not need MySQL for a single-operator lab login.</li>
    <li>Keep one schema file. PHP and Python must insert the same columns or sessions will not match.</li>
    <li>Hash passwords with PBKDF2-SHA256. Do not store plaintext and do not print hashes in logs.</li>
    <li>Gate dashboard and account pages on a database session cookie, not a hidden form field.</li>
    <li>RTF, DOC, and XHTML are operator documents. They are not part of the login path.</li>
  </ul>
  <h2>Commands</h2>
  <p><code>python3 site/login/tools/init_auth_db.py init</code></p>
  <p><code>python3 site/login/tools/init_auth_db.py seed --password LabOnly1234</code></p>
  <p><code>python3 site/login/tools/login_server.py --host 127.0.0.1 --port 8088</code></p>
</body>
</html>
